      "Expo '74 was opened by President Richard Nixon, and some 5.2 million visitors came. Its theme, celebrating the fresh new environment, was the first environmental theme for a world's fair. The US Pavilion, with its distinctive cable-supported roof, still stands in Riverfront Park, and a giant garbage-eating goat sculpture, built for the fair, still swallows trash in the park today.",
