      "Robert Louis Stevenson came to California to marry Fanny Osbourne, an American woman he had met in France. Poor and in poor health, the couple spent their honeymoon in 1880 in an abandoned miners' bunkhouse on Mount St. Helena, and Stevenson wrote about the experience in The Silverado Squatters. He visited local winemakers and wrote warmly of their efforts to find the best soils for each grape.",
