      winter: "The high season — afternoons near 21°C, nights around 8°C, and sunshine almost every day, with snow gleaming on the summit of San Jacinto above the palms. A few Pacific storms bring the year's little rain. Snowbirds fill the resorts and golf courses, and Modernism Week fills the town in February.",
      spring: "Warm and windy — afternoons climbing from about 26°C in March to 35°C by late May, wildflowers blooming in the desert after wet winters, and strong winds blowing through the San Gorgonio Pass, spinning the thousands of wind turbines that line it. The music festivals at nearby Indio draw huge crowds in April.",
      summer: "Brutally hot — afternoons near 41°C and often well above 45°C, nights that barely fall below 25°C, and sunshine every day. Locals stay indoors or head up the aerial tramway to the cool forests on the mountain above. The occasional monsoon surge brings humidity and a dramatic thunderstorm.",
